      "text": "FOUNDATIONS\n\nEverything here is read out of the live app: colour and size tokens come from src/styles/tokens/tokens.json (sourced from Figma), the shadow, motion and type-composition layers are hand-authored alongside it.\n\nNothing on this page is a proposal — it is what ships today."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-components",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -420,
      "w": 640,
      "text": "COMPONENTS\n\nEach artboard renders the real CSS: design/canvas/_app.css is copied verbatim from src/styles/app.css by design/canvas/sync-app-css.mjs, so these can't quietly drift from the app.\n\nStates that are normally hover/active pseudo-classes are rendered as separate instances (marked DEFAULT / HOVER / PRESSED / FOCUS) so you can see all of them at once instead of hunting for them."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-screens",
      "page": "page-3",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -340,
      "w": 620,
      "text": "SCREENS\n\nTen screens at 390 × 844, built from the same component CSS rather than redrawn. Content is representative, not live — the deck, counts and streak are plausible sample data.\n\nEach screen is shown in the state worth looking at: Add a word in the two-candidate ambiguity, Add from text mid-read, the dashboard with work to do."
    }
